From bdd9ef45b7de0301f348aa5342cbcc67ef0c716f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Durham <adn@x>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:50:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hyundai: FCA11-long - delete the 2.5 s actuation budget and
 the 3 s cooldown (0035)

The owner saw "about 2 seconds of braking per event". That was OUR limit, not the ESC: the panda's FCA11-long TX
hook capped a continuous actuation episode at 2.5 s (HYUNDAI_FCA11_LONG_MAX_ACT_US), then REFUSED all new
actuation for 3 s (HYUNDAI_FCA11_LONG_COOLDOWN_US). The car layer mirrored both and deliberately stopped commanding
at the budget edge. Route 151 (the first drive with 0030 live): 54 of 77 normal-driving episodes were clipped exactly
at 2.5 s, 45 of them while the planner was still asking to brake (68.5 s of live demand dropped), 37 mid-stop. 30 of
the 31 refused 0x38D frames on that drive are the 2.5 s edge frame.

The budget only ever bounded a live-but-wedged host. That case is covered without it: the 30 LSB (0.30 g) cap, the
+4 LSB per accepted frame rate limit, the 100 ms stale-TX hand-back, the heartbeat, the driver-cut latch, the
camera-owns hand-back and - decisively - braking is kinematically self-terminating (it drives the slowest wheel
below the 9 km/h floor, where every actuating frame is refused). Any cap below that time truncates real stops; any
cap above it is dead code. A 2.5 s cap with a 3 s refusal window after it was the worst of both.

Panda (opendbc/safety/modes/hyundai.h):
  * DELETED: MAX_ACT_US, COOLDOWN_US, act_active, ts_act, ts_act_end and the whole budget/cooldown block.
  * ONSET rule (the one control change): the rate-limit reference is 0 - so the frame is capped at RATE_STEP
    (4 LSB) - whenever the ESC is not currently seeing our command: no accepted frame this arm, the last
    accepted frame was PASSIVE (already true before 0035: a passive frame stores dec_last = 0), or our stream
    went STALE past TX_STALE (NEW: the same predicate hyundai_fwd_hook uses to forward the camera again).
    Without the stale term a host could brake at 30, go silent > 100 ms (camera re-owns, ESC sees 0) and reopen
    at 30 - a 0 -> 30 step at the ESC that the cooldown used to space out and that would now be unbounded.
    The ramp law, the 30 LSB cap, the speed floor, the driver-cut latch and camera-owns are UNCHANGED.

Car layer (opendbc/sunnypilot/car/hyundai/fca11_long.py):
  * DELETED: FCA11_BUDGET_FRAMES / FCA11_COOLDOWN_FRAMES / FCA11_COOLDOWN_MARGIN_FRAMES, the _in_budget /
    _budget_start / _budget_end mirror, the budget-edge stop-commanding, the cooldown hold-off and the cooldown
    stamping on echo-confirmed passive frames.
  * KEPT: the passive close frame on every braking true -> false edge (the clean hand-back), the echo re-owe of a
    refused close frame (now never while braking again - re-owing then would cut the live brake for a slot).
    The only remaining hold-off is close-frame ORDERING: an owed passive frame goes out first, so a re-brake
    waits at most one 50 Hz send slot (<= 20 ms).

Cal tool (opendbc/sunnypilot/car/hyundai/cal_mode.py, replaces 0031's predicate):
  * arming is budget-free under the existing conditions;
  * CAL_MAX_HOLD_S = 10 s: a rep with a longer (or non-positive / unparseable) hold is refused, never armed;
  * a tool-side WATCHDOG in Fca11LongBrake drops any scripted ask held > CAL_MAX_HOLD_S + 0.2 s, forces the
    production release (passive close frame), records the rep 'watchdog' (not ok) and never re-arms it this
    session. It bounds only the scripted ask - a planner ask is never silenced by it.

Evidence (car-features/fca11-budget-removal/REPORT.md): panda suite 12 test functions red -> green, 273 unchanged
green; car layer 12 red -> green, 83 unchanged green; real compiled-safety replay of route 151, old vs new in
lock-step: 11 240 host frames, 30 REFUSED -> SENT (all budget-expiry only), 0 SENT -> REFUSED.
